# UST.G3BA Common-Fiber Face-Cover Topological Gram Theorem

## Purpose

The selected three-cycle calculation has two realizations. The regauged
Ehresmann campaign transports actual Morse spheres into the common
`lambda=0` fiber, while G3AT transports their polarized Gauss-Manin lines.
G3BA binds these realizations along the same B97 critical points and B98
paths and extracts the Gram decision topologically. It does not reduce
floating or interval-complex coordinates modulo 101.

## Exact theorem

Assume that each selected A1 Morse sphere has an exact prefix-free dyadic
cover of all eight oriented octahedral faces after transport to the common
fiber. Assume also that for every cell from two distinct cycles, at least one
of the five complex endpoint coordinates has disjoint real or imaginary Arb
intervals.

Then the three compact images are pairwise disjoint. Their cross-intersection
numbers are therefore zero. The hash-bound B87 saturation theorem already
certifies that every selected A1 sphere is an integral primitive minus-two
class. Geometrically, its oriented normal Euler number is

```text
-chi(S2) = -2.
```

Consequently the integral Gram matrix is

```text
G = -2 I3,
det(G) = -8,
rank_Q(G) = 3.
```

The three classes are rationally independent. By B96, this selected
three-node subsystem cannot detect the nonsplit affine class: it has no cycle
relation on which a relation defect could be nonzero.

The de Rham and Betti conclusions agree because Gauss-Manin and Ehresmann
transport are the two realizations of the same flat local system along the
same hash-bound paths. In the resulting three-line span, the G3AW reflections
are the three coordinate sign changes. No B103 coordinate evaluation is
needed to decide independence.

## Strict execution boundary

A partial campaign may be audited, but it cannot emit the theorem. Promotion
requires all three checkpoints to be `COMPLETE`, all eight face covers to be
exact, all source hashes and the kernel-model hash to agree, and every
cross-cycle cell pair to have a strict interval-separation witness.

If complete covers contain nonseparated boxes, G3BA does not call them
intersections. Those boxes must be refined or subjected to an oriented
intersection root-isolation calculation.

The frozen partial audit currently contains `273`, `250` and `276` certified
cells. All `212,598` cross-cycle cell pairs are separated. More strongly, the
same serialized `Re(q[2])` component orders the three partial images strictly as

```text
cycle 1 < cycle 3 < cycle 2.
```

Several additional scalar components separate each pair. This is useful
evidence that the completed campaign will close by disjointness, but no bound
on an uncovered cell is inferred from its neighbors.

G3BA does not close `B.ETA9.01`. A passing result retires only the present
three-node detector and forces a deliberate enlargement of the finite B96
subsystem. It emits neither rank-1509 integral coordinates nor 248 period
values.

